{% markdown %}

The site just had a substantial overhaul: upgraded to Eleventy v3, dropped Gulp and upstream VF CSS, and pared things down to a clean Eleventy + Sass + esbuild setup. Pages should load a bit faster and the codebase is much easier to work with.

> #### tl;dr
>
> - Eleventy v3 upgrade and a simpler build.
> - Removed Gulp and upstream Visual Framework CSS; kept local SCSS and templates.
> - Added a tiny shim for common `vf-*` classes still used in templates.
> - Images and the search index now build via Eleventy-integrated scripts.
> - CI/build is streamlined; local `yarn dev` stays snappy.

### Why change

I’m no longer closely involved with VF, and the Gulp-based pipeline added complexity I no longer need. The goal: keep the bits I use (templates, local styles), remove the rest, and modernize the build with Eleventy v3.

### What changed

- Build and tooling
  - Switched to Eleventy v3.
  - Replaced Gulp with Eleventy + Dart Sass + esbuild.
  - CI builds with a single `yarn build` that outputs to `build/`.

- CSS and templates
  - Kept local SCSS and components.
  - Refactored SCSS in-place: replaced `meta.load-css` with `@use`, centralized breakpoints, flattened deep nesting.
  - Tightened Stylelint rules (max nesting; selector complexity) to keep CSS maintainable.
  - Removed legacy `{% raw %}{% render %}{% endraw %}`/`codeblock` usage and their shims; converted posts to plain HTML or fenced code.

- Eleventy-integrated tasks
  - Images: `scripts/process-images.js` (sharp) runs on build and during dev.
  - Search: `scripts/build-search-index.js` regenerates the client-side index on build.
  - Cleaned passthroughs; removed unused VF assets.

If you want the gory details, the changelog in the pull request has the blow-by-blow: [Feat/update to 11ty v3 + move away from VF (PR #12)](https://github.com/khawkins98/allaboutken-11ty/pull/12).

