### Dev notes (for future me, or you)

- Eleventy config lives in `eleventy.js`.
- Styles start at `src/components/vf-componenet-rollup/index.scss` with local packages like `vf-local-overrides/` and `vf-font-now-alt/`.
- Legacy `vf-*` classes get enough styling from `_vf-shim.scss` to keep layouts intact.
- During `yarn dev`, Eleventy watches templates; Sass and esbuild handle CSS/JS; images auto-process.

### Refactor highlights

- Replaced `@include meta.load-css` with `@use … as *` for `normalize` and content styling.
- Centralized all breakpoints in `_settings.scss` and kept media queries in Sass.
- Flattened deep selector nesting; enforced max nesting via Stylelint.
- Converted `{% raw %}{% codeblock %}{% endraw %}` to fenced code; removed the shim.
- Removed legacy `{% raw %}{% render %}{% endraw %}` usages and tag; switched to plain HTML patterns.
- Deleted `temp-fixes/vf-extensions/` and unused passthroughs.

### What’s next

- Prune unused CSS selectors and consolidate utilities.
- Consider `@11ty/eleventy-img` for responsive images.
- Document the SCSS conventions and refactor summary in `README.md`.

Thanks for reading—and if you spot anything odd post‑migration, please let me know.

